module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.RationalEquivalenceDefs
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Intersection.TorFormula.IntersectionMultiplicity
public import
  StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Intersection.TorFormulaMultiplicities.TransversalIntersection
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Support.TestModuleStalk
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Variety.Smooth.SmoothLocus

/-!
# A component of multiplicity one of a proper intersection

Let `X` be a nonsingular variety over a perfect field `k`, let `V`, `W ⊆ X` be closed subschemes
which intersect properly, and let `Z` be an irreducible component of `V ∩ W` whose multiplicity
in the closed subscheme `V ∩ W` is one. Then the intersection multiplicity is
`e(X, V · W, Z) = 1`, and `V` and `W` are smooth in a general point of `Z`.

Both conclusions are read at the generic point `ξ` of `Z`. The local ring `A = 𝒪_{X, ξ}` is
regular, the two subschemes induce the ideals `I = 𝓘_{V, ξ}` and `J = 𝓘_{W, ξ}` of `A`, and the
multiplicity-one hypothesis says that `A ⧸ (I ⊔ J)`, the local ring of `V ∩ W` at `ξ`, is the
residue field. The two ideals are then generated by complementary parts of a single regular system
of parameters of `A`, so `A ⧸ I` and `A ⧸ J` are regular local rings and the alternating sum of
the lengths of the modules `Tor_i^A(A ⧸ I, A ⧸ J)`, which is `e(X, V · W, Z)`, is one. Since
`A ⧸ I` is the local ring of `V` at `ξ` and the ground field is perfect, `V` is smooth at `ξ`;
the smooth locus is open, so `V` is smooth on a neighbourhood of `ξ` in `X`, hence on a dense
open subset of `Z`. The same applies to `W`, and intersecting the two neighbourhoods gives a
single open set on which both are smooth.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.intersectionMultiplicity_eq_one_and_exists_isOpen_smoothAt`: both
  conclusions of Stacks 0B1I, at the generic point of the component.
* `intersectionMultiplicity_eq_one_and_exists_isOpen_smoothAt_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one`, in
  the same namespace: the two conclusions with the multiplicity-one hypothesis read as the
  colength of the join of the two local ideals.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isOpen_smoothAt_of_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_stalk`: a closed
  subscheme whose local ring at a point is regular is smooth on a neighbourhood of that point.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.componentMultiplicity_subschemeι_eq_toNat_length_quotient_stalk`: the
  multiplicity of a component of a closed subscheme is the colength of the stalk of its ideal
  sheaf at the generic point.

## Implementation notes

The component `Z` is given by its generic point `ζ` of `(𝓘_V ⊔ 𝓘_W).subscheme`, the
scheme-theoretic intersection `V ∩ W`, and its multiplicity in `V ∩ W` is
`Stacks.Chow.componentMultiplicity` of Tag 02QU, the length of the local ring of `V ∩ W` at `ζ`
over the local ring of `X`. That length is the colength of `I ⊔ J` because the local ring of a
closed subscheme is the quotient of the ambient local ring by the stalk of its ideal sheaf
(`AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.subschemeStalkQuotLinearEquiv`) and the stalk of a join of
ideal sheaves is the join of the stalks (`AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_sup`).

The multiplicity `e(X, V · W, Z)` is `Stacks.Intersection.intersectionMultiplicity` of Tag 0AZR,
whose value at `ξ` is by definition the Tor-formula multiplicity
`Ideal.localIntersectionMultiplicity` of the pair `(I, A ⧸ J)`, so the computation of Tag 0B1I is
the one of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Intersection.TorFormulaMultiplicities.TransversalIntersection`.

As in that module, the hypotheses on the ambient variety are the ones the proof consumes at `ξ`:
regularity of `𝒪_{X, ξ}`, which nonsingularity of `X` provides at every point, and the local form
`dim A ≤ dim (A ⧸ I) + dim (A ⧸ J)` of proper intersection, which the source derives from the
global dimension inequality through the dimension formula of Varieties, Lemma 0B2J. Neither
irreducibility nor reducedness of `V` and `W` is used, so they are arbitrary closed subschemes.

Smoothness is the pointwise predicate `AlgebraicGeometry.InfinitesimalLifting.SmoothAt` for the
structure morphism of the subscheme, and "smooth in a general point of `Z`" is delivered as an
open `U ⊆ X` containing `ξ` such that every point of `V` and of `W` lying over `U` is a smooth
point: as `ξ` is the generic point of `Z`, such a `U` meets `Z` in a dense open subset.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B1I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B1I)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AZR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AZR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02QU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02QU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8X](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8X)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### Smoothness near a point whose local ring is regular -/

/-- The local ring of the closed subscheme cut out by an ideal sheaf is regular as soon as the
quotient of the ambient local ring by the stalk of the ideal sheaf is regular. -/
theorem isRegularLocalRing_stalk_subscheme_of_isRegularLocalRing_quotient {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (z : I.subscheme)
    (h : IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι z) ⧸
      IdealSheafData.stalk I (I.subschemeι z))) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (I.subscheme.presheaf.stalk z) :=
  let := h
  IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv (IdealSheafData.subschemeStalkQuotEquiv I z)

/-- **A closed subscheme is smooth near a point with regular local ring.** Let `X` be a scheme
locally of finite type over a perfect field `k` and let `I` be a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals
on `X`. If the quotient of `𝒪_{X, x}` by the stalk of `I` is a regular local ring at a point `x`
of the closed subscheme cut out by `I`, then that subscheme is smooth over `k` at each of its
points lying over some open neighbourhood of `x` in `X`. -/
@[sga "1 II 5.4" "more general", sga "7 XVI 1.3" "more general"]
theorem exists_isOpen_smoothAt_of_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_stalk (k : Type u) [Field k]
    [PerfectField k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType p]
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (z : I.subscheme)
    (h : IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι z) ⧸
      IdealSheafData.stalk I (I.subschemeι z))) :
    ∃ U : X.Opens, I.subschemeι z ∈ U ∧
      ∀ v : I.subscheme, I.subschemeι v ∈ U →
        InfinitesimalLifting.SmoothAt (I.subschemeι ≫ p) v := by
  have hz : z ∈ {y : I.subscheme | IsRegularLocalRing (I.subscheme.presheaf.stalk y)} :=
    isRegularLocalRing_stalk_subscheme_of_isRegularLocalRing_quotient I z h
  rw [← smoothAt_locus_eq_regular_locus k (I.subschemeι ≫ p)] at hz
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hUeq⟩ :=
    I.subschemeι.isClosedEmbedding.isInducing.isOpen_iff.mp
      (isOpen_smoothAt_locus (I.subschemeι ≫ p))
  exact ⟨⟨U, hU⟩, hUeq.symm.subset hz, fun v hv => hUeq.subset hv⟩

/-! ### The two conclusions at a component of multiplicity one -/

/-- The multiplicity of an irreducible component of the closed subscheme cut out by an ideal
sheaf is the colength of the stalk of that ideal sheaf at the component's generic point. -/
theorem componentMultiplicity_subschemeι_eq_toNat_length_quotient_stalk {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (ζ : genericPoints I.subscheme) :
    Stacks.Chow.componentMultiplicity I.subschemeι ζ =
      ((Module.length (X.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι ζ.1))
        (X.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι ζ.1) ⧸
          IdealSheafData.stalk I (I.subschemeι ζ.1))).toNat : ℤ) := by
  let : Module (X.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι ζ.1)) (I.subscheme.presheaf.stalk ζ.1) :=
    Module.compHom (I.subscheme.presheaf.stalk ζ.1) (I.subschemeι.stalkMap ζ.1).hom
  have hlen := (IdealSheafData.subschemeStalkQuotLinearEquiv I ζ.1).length_eq
  dsimp only [Stacks.Chow.componentMultiplicity]
  exact congrArg (fun n : ℕ∞ => (n.toNat : ℤ)) hlen.symm

/-- **The two conclusions of Stacks 0B1I, with the multiplicity-one hypothesis in local form.**
At a point `x` of both closed subschemes at which the local ring of `X` is regular, the two local
ideals have residue field as common quotient and the intersection is proper, the intersection
multiplicity at `x` is one and both subschemes are smooth over `k` on a neighbourhood of `x`. -/
theorem intersectionMultiplicity_eq_one_and_exists_isOpen_smoothAt_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one
    (k : Type u) [Field k] [PerfectField k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [LocallyOfFiniteType p] (IV IW : X.IdealSheafData) (x : X)
    (hX : IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x))
    (hxV : x ∈ IV.support) (hxW : x ∈ IW.support)
    (hlen : Module.length (X.presheaf.stalk x)
      (X.presheaf.stalk x ⧸ (IdealSheafData.stalk IV x ⊔ IdealSheafData.stalk IW x)) = 1)
    (hproper : ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk x) ≤
      ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk x ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk IV x) +
        ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk x ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk IW x)) :
    Stacks.Intersection.intersectionMultiplicity IV IW x = 1 ∧
      ∃ U : X.Opens, x ∈ U ∧
        (∀ v : IV.subscheme, IV.subschemeι v ∈ U →
          InfinitesimalLifting.SmoothAt (IV.subschemeι ≫ p) v) ∧
        (∀ w : IW.subscheme, IW.subschemeι w ∈ U →
          InfinitesimalLifting.SmoothAt (IW.subschemeι ≫ p) w) := by
  let := hX
  refine ⟨IsRegularLocalRing.localIntersectionMultiplicity_eq_one_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one
    (IdealSheafData.stalk IV x) (IdealSheafData.stalk IW x) hlen hproper, ?_⟩
  have hregI : IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk IV x) :=
    IsRegularLocalRing.isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one
      (IdealSheafData.stalk IV x) (IdealSheafData.stalk IW x) hlen hproper
  have hregJ : IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk IW x) :=
    IsRegularLocalRing.isRegularLocalRing_quotient_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one
      (IdealSheafData.stalk IW x) (IdealSheafData.stalk IV x)
      (by rw [sup_comm]; exact hlen) (by rw [add_comm]; exact hproper)
  obtain ⟨U₁, hx₁, hsmoothV⟩ := exists_isOpen_smoothAt_of_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_stalk k p IV
    (IdealSheafData.subschemePoint IV x hxV) hregI
  obtain ⟨U₂, hx₂, hsmoothW⟩ := exists_isOpen_smoothAt_of_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_stalk k p IW
    (IdealSheafData.subschemePoint IW x hxW) hregJ
  exact ⟨U₁ ⊓ U₂, ⟨hx₁, hx₂⟩, fun v hv => hsmoothV v hv.1, fun w hw => hsmoothW w hw.2⟩

/-- **Stacks 0B1I.** Let `X` be a nonsingular variety over a perfect field `k`, let `V` and `W` be
the closed subschemes of `X` cut out by the quasi-coherent sheaves of ideals `IV` and `IW`, and
let `ζ` be the generic point of an irreducible component `Z` of the scheme-theoretic intersection
`V ∩ W`, with image `ξ` in `X`. Assume that `V` and `W` intersect properly along `Z`, in the local
form `dim 𝒪_{X, ξ} ≤ dim 𝒪_{V, ξ} + dim 𝒪_{W, ξ}`, and that the multiplicity of `Z` in `V ∩ W`
is one. Then the intersection multiplicity is `e(X, V · W, Z) = 1`, and there is an open
neighbourhood of `ξ` in `X` over which both `V` and `W` are smooth: `V` and `W` are smooth in a
general point of `Z`. -/
@[stacks 0B1I "both conclusions, at the generic point of the component"]
theorem intersectionMultiplicity_eq_one_and_exists_isOpen_smoothAt (k : Type u) [Field k]
    [PerfectField k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType p]
    (IV IW : X.IdealSheafData) (ζ : genericPoints (IV ⊔ IW).subscheme)
    (hX : IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk ((IV ⊔ IW).subschemeι ζ.1)))
    (hproper : ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk ((IV ⊔ IW).subschemeι ζ.1)) ≤
      ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk ((IV ⊔ IW).subschemeι ζ.1) ⧸
          IdealSheafData.stalk IV ((IV ⊔ IW).subschemeι ζ.1)) +
        ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk ((IV ⊔ IW).subschemeι ζ.1) ⧸
          IdealSheafData.stalk IW ((IV ⊔ IW).subschemeι ζ.1)))
    (hmult : Stacks.Chow.componentMultiplicity (IV ⊔ IW).subschemeι ζ = 1) :
    Stacks.Intersection.intersectionMultiplicity IV IW ((IV ⊔ IW).subschemeι ζ.1) = 1 ∧
      ∃ U : X.Opens, (IV ⊔ IW).subschemeι ζ.1 ∈ U ∧
        (∀ v : IV.subscheme, IV.subschemeι v ∈ U →
          InfinitesimalLifting.SmoothAt (IV.subschemeι ≫ p) v) ∧
        (∀ w : IW.subscheme, IW.subschemeι w ∈ U →
          InfinitesimalLifting.SmoothAt (IW.subschemeι ≫ p) w) := by
  classical
  have hcm := componentMultiplicity_subschemeι_eq_toNat_length_quotient_stalk (IV ⊔ IW) ζ
  rw [hmult, IdealSheafData.stalk_sup] at hcm
  have hlen := (ENat.toNat_eq_iff one_ne_zero).1
    (Nat.cast_injective (R := ℤ) (by simpa using hcm.symm))
  have hsupp : (IV ⊔ IW).subschemeι ζ.1 ∈ (IV ⊔ IW).support := ζ.1.2
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_sup] at hsupp
  exact intersectionMultiplicity_eq_one_and_exists_isOpen_smoothAt_of_length_quotient_sup_eq_one
    k p IV IW _ hX hsupp.1 hsupp.2 hlen hproper

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
